TSCOS – Traffic Signal Control Operating System

A working model of the **Traffic Signal Control Operating System (TSCOS)** from the
OS mini-project *"Design and Development of a Traffic Signal Control Operating System for
Smart Junction Management"*.

Each approach of a four-way junction (North, South, East, West) is a **process** that
competes for a shared resource, the **green signal**, which plays the role of CPU time.
The model applies classic OS ideas:

| OS concept | Use in TSCOS |
|---|---|
| Priority scheduling | Manual override > Emergency > Pedestrian > Adaptive density |
| Round-robin scheduling | Equal traffic: fixed 20 s slots in order N → E → S → W |
| Mutual exclusion (mutex) | `intersection_lock` – only one approach may be green |
| Safe state transitions | Every green goes GREEN → YELLOW (5 s) → RED |
| Process control block | `PCB` record per lane |
| IPC | `Shared` structure written by sensors, read by the scheduler |

